+// ---- the coin / credit path -----------------------------------------------------------
+// The ST-V BIOS owns coins. Its per-frame service *0x06000610 (ROM 0x30114, run from RAM
+// 0x06000D14) samples the coin switches (PORTC bits 0/1) and accrues credits in backup RAM;
+// the cart never sees a coin. It sees only the credit count and per-player start code in
+// the 0x06000660 panel report (stv_panel_read), and it calls *0x06000664(player) to take one
+// credit when START is pressed (func_0220f9d4, func_0220600e). The factory default is a
+// common coin chute, 1 coin = 1 credit, so both slots feed one pool and a coin is accepted
