+// ST-V SYSTEM-BIOS LAYER: the system words the real BIOS (US epr-17952a) maintains in work
+// RAM, decoded from its disassembly (port/run/P45/bios_dis.txt) and checked against MAME 0.285.
+//   0x06000798  BIOS settings word, copied from backup RAM at boot. Factory default
+//               0x000808FD: bit5 (0x20) set = the cart runs its own attract, START and
+//               game-over loop (func_02201590 clears 0x060987D0, func_022016ac state 4 loops
+//               to state 1); clear = multi-cart rotation owned by the BIOS (state 4 calls
+//               *0x0600060C). bit6 (0x40) = sound. main_stv.cpp seeds it.
+//   0x06000654  multi-cart join-countdown word, written by the BIOS only when bit5 is clear;
+//               the cart reads it only on that path (func_022058a8, func_0220600e).
+//   0x06000728  system-switch record (COIN1/2, TEST, SERVICE, START1/2), published every
+//               VBlank in stv_scene_probe_tick. The cart derives its edge word 0x06098798.
+//   credits     held by the BIOS (deliver_coin), reported by 0x06000660, taken by 0x06000664.
+// 0x06000640 is modelled as a free-running frame timer (the real one reads a backup-RAM
+// counter). STV_NOSYSBIOS disables the per-frame tick for A/B checks.
+static bool stv_sysbios_on() {
+    static bool v = (std::getenv("STV_NOSYSBIOS") == nullptr);
+    return v;
